    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00064",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "When a connection is available, [A60][I61]select[/I61]()[/A60] indicates that the file descriptor for\nthe socket is ready for reading.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A60": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/select.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I61": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00065",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Many socket options are described as having implementation-defined default values, which may differ according to the protocol in\nuse by the socket. Existing practice differs on whether socket options such as SO_SNDBUF that were customized on the original\nlistening socket will impact the corresponding option on the newly returned socket. Implementations are permitted to allow\ninheritance of customized settings where it makes sense, although the most portable approach for applications is to limit [A62][I63]setsockopt[/I63]()[/A62] customizations to only the accepted socket.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A62": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/setsockopt.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I63": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00066",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     5
    ],
    "text": "For AF_UNIX sockets, it is recommended that [I64]address[/I64] points to a buffer of length greater than [CODE65] which has been initialized with null bytes. That way, even if the implementation supports the use of all bytes of\n[I66]sun_path[/I66] without a terminating null byte, the larger buffer guarantees that the [I67]sun_path[/I67] member can then be passed to\nother interfaces that expect a null-terminated string. If no truncation occurred based on the input value of [I68]address_len[/I68], it\nis unspecified whether the returned [I69]address_len[/I69] will be [CODE70], or merely a value at least as\nlarge as [CODE71] plus the number of non-null bytes stored in [I72]sun_path[/I72].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I64": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE65": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>sizeof(struct\nsockaddr_un)</tt>"
     },
     "I66": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I67": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I68": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I69": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE70": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>sizeof(struct sockaddr_un)</tt>"
     },
     "CODE71": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>offsetof(struct sockaddr_un, sun_path)</tt>"
     },
     "I72": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00067",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A73][/A73]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A73": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_06_08\" id=\"tag_17_06_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00068",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The SOCK_CLOEXEC and SOCK_CLOFORK flags of [I74]accept4[/I74]() are necessary to avoid a data race in multi-threaded applications.\nWithout SOCK_CLOFORK, a file descriptor is leaked into a child process created by one thread in the window between another thread\ncreating a file descriptor with [I75]accept[/I75]() and then using [A76][I77]fcntl[/I77]()[/A76] to set the\nFD_CLOFORK flag. Without SOCK_CLOEXEC, a file descriptor intentionally inherited by child processes is similarly leaked into an\nexecuted program if FD_CLOEXEC is not set atomically.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I74": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I75": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A76": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I77": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00069",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Two designs often used for network servers are multi-threaded servers with a pre-created pool of worker threads, where the\nthread that accepts the connection request hands over the new file descriptor to a worker thread for servicing, and pre-fork\nservers with a pre-created pool of worker processes, where the process that accepts the connection request passes the new file\ndescriptor (for example via [A78][I79]sendmsg[/I79]()[/A78]) to a worker process. In both of these\ndesigns, [I80]accept4[/I80]() should be used with the SOCK_CLOFORK flag set. Simpler designs are also sometimes used that do not\npre-create a pool. For a multi-threaded server that creates a thread to handle each request, SOCK_CLOFORK should still be used. For\na forking server that creates a child to service each request, clearly SOCK_CLOFORK cannot be used if the child is to inherit the\nfile descriptor to be serviced, and therefore this type of server needs to use an alternative method of indicating the end of\ncommunications, for example using [A81][I82]shutdown[/I82]()[/A81], to ensure the client sees\nend-of-file, rather than just closing the socket. Such child processes should set FD_CLOFORK on the inherited file descriptor\nbefore they attempt to start any additional child processes to avoid leakage into those children.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A78": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sendmsg.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I79": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I80": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A81": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/shutdown.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I82": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00070",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The SOCK_NONBLOCK flag is for convenience in avoiding additional [A83][I84]fcntl[/I84]()[/A83] calls, as\nwell as providing specific control over the O_NONBLOCK flag, since traditional implementations of [I85]accept[/I85]() differ on whether\nO_NONBLOCK is inherited from the [I86]socket[/I86] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A83": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I84": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I85": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I86": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
